+# Brief — PM, `fix/tally-absent-vs-wrong`
+
+**From** `pij-mental-dajeil` (o-prime, `AI-Substrate/dd`) · 2026-08-14
+**You are the PM.** You own the plan, the fleet, the evidence and the landing.
+**You do NOT implement.** Your operating contract is
+`/Users/jordanknight/substrate/dd/.harness/government/how-fleets-work.md` — read it first.
+
+## The tree
+
+Worktree `/Users/jordanknight/substrate/dd-worktrees/tally-absent`, branch
+`fix/tally-absent-vs-wrong`, rebased onto `969a359` (current main), clean, deps installed,
+built. **Cite line numbers only from THIS tree.**
+
+The binary is now **`ddocs`**, not `dd` — it was renamed today because `dd` shadowed POSIX
+`dd(1)`. `ddocs` is also globally linked, so bare `ddocs …` works anywhere.
+
+## The defect — reproduced by me on this exact tree
+
+A hand-authored document (one a person writes in an editor, never passed through a writer
+verb) against a tally-marked schema is **refused by `ddocs validate`**:
+
+```
+status: error  code: E463
+  $.sections[rows].value[0].t | stored tally says undefined but the rows sum to 15
+  $.sections[rows].tally.a    | stored tally says undefined but the rows sum to 10
+  $.sections[rows].tally.b    | stored tally says undefined but the rows sum to 5
+  $.sections[rows].tally.t    | stored tally says undefined but the rows sum to 15
+```
+
+Touch it with any writer (`ddocs set …` on an unrelated field) and it goes `ok`.
+
+**Mechanism, in `src/core/tally.ts`**: `tallyMismatches` compares stored against computed
+with `Object.is` at two sites — the row-total loop and the footer loop. When nothing is
+stored, `held`/`row[total]` is `undefined`, `Object.is(undefined, 15)` is false, and
+**absence takes the mismatch branch. There is no third branch.**
+
+**It conflates ABSENT with WRONG.** Nothing is stored, so nothing contradicts the rows.
+
+## The ruling — already made, do not re-open it
+
+**Per-cell: report a mismatch ONLY where a value is STORED and disagrees. Never report
+absence, at either site.** No new state, no inferring written-ness.
+
+Four cases, all of which must hold:
+
+| case | required behaviour |
+|---|---|
+| nothing stored | silent |
+| partial footer (`tally: {a: 10}`, correct; `b`/`t` absent) | only the stored cell checked |
+| hand-author filled row totals themselves, correct, no footer | silent — they ARE stored, so checked, and they agree |
+| stored and WRONG (`tally.a: 99` vs true 10) | reported, unchanged |
+
+**Why "absent is fine only until first write" was rejected**: a hand-author who computes
+their own row totals produces a document **byte-identical** to one whose footer was deleted
+after a write. No signal separates them, so that rule would report an honest author as a
+liar. A validator that cannot distinguish two states must not report either.
+
+## Non-vacuity — the part most likely to be got wrong
+
+A fix that silenced *everything* would pass a test that only checks the four spurious errors
+disappeared. **The negation proof must plant a WRONG STORED value and confirm it still
+reports.** Cover all four rows of the table above as separate assertions.
+
+Dim-0: break the WORLD the test watches, not the test.
+
+## Why this is urgent
+
+It blocks the docs phase. Every worked example we print is by definition hand-authored, so a
+cold reader following our own how-to gets four ERRORs on their first document — our front
+door contradicting our guide. Two external consumers (a novels repo, `osk-data`) hand-author
+their first documents too.
+
+## Scope fence
+
+`src/core/tally.ts` + its tests. **Do not** touch the render path, the write path, or
+`dd build`. **No `--fix` flag** — validate reports, writers repair. If you reach for one,
+stop and come back to me.
+
+## Standing constraints
+
+- **No push, no PR, no tag, no release without my word.**
+- Never read or write `.the-flow-state.json`, `the-flow.json`, `the-flow.md`.
+- **Constraint 10 — never tear a seat down by pane id.** A reboot reissued tmux pane ids, so
+  stale descriptors name live panes they do not own; a close-by-pane can kill an unrelated
+  seat, including me. The discriminator is **PID, checked at execution time**, never read
+  from the descriptor.
+- Full gate under a **clean HOME** before you accept anything: a developer `HOME` carrying
+  `~/.dd` schemas fails a test CI cannot see (backlog 25).
+- Count verdicts **at the head you pushed**, with the denominator.
+- `npm` here resolves through a **corporate supply-chain proxy**. Never pass a public
+  `--registry` and never edit a `resolved` URL — see `AGENTS.md`, first sections.
+
+## Your fleet — Jordan's choice, spawn them yourself
+
+Coder **`claude-opus-5`**, reviewer **`gpt-5.6-terra`**, both `--harness pi --bin omp`.
+All three seats share **your window**. Discover ids with `pij models`, canary before
+dispatch (model, effort, identity, cwd, branch), persist the roster before you dispatch.
+The reviewer is acquired **lazily at first REVIEW** — do not pre-spawn it.
+
+Report at both edges. Escalate anything that changes the shape of the work.
